{"resourceIdentifier":"3019","resourceName":"REGENERATING DEGRADED LANDS IN FLORIDA THROUGH PONGAMIA","description":"This grouped project aims to reforest and restore degraded agricultural lands by planting Pongamia trees. Reforestation started in 2018, through the planting of 100 to 145 Pongamia  trees per acre (250 to 360 trees per hectare, approximately). The project aims to increase the Pongamia plantation area to 1,000 ha and certify carbon offsets for a period of 20 years following the small-scale afforestation and reforestation methodology (VCS - AR-AMS0007). \r\nRegenerative agriculture is a system of growing food that reverses climate change by revitalizing natural ecosystems and agricultural lands while improving water quality and soil biodiversity. It improves the health of soils capable of producing high quality, nutrient dense food. Currently, the project areas are in a high state of degradation due to intensive agriculture practices. Although the project represents an intervention on the ground, it favors the increase and recovery of land that enhances the possibility of connecting fragments of forest, reducing fertilization use and providing an additional source of income to the landowners.","location":{"latitude":27.301358,"longitude":-80.595833},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-06-21","endExclusive":"2022-07-22","endInclusive":"2022-07-21"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"3019"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"FL"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Multiple Proponents"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3019"},{"type":"bufferSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"3019"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"4133"}]},{"co